Metric Category,Metric Name,Value,Description,Interpretation
Core Quality,Composite Quality Score,0.820000,"Overall clustering quality (0-1, higher is better)","Excellent >0.8, Good >0.6, Fair >0.4, Poor <0.4"
Core Quality,Silhouette Score,0.480000,Cluster separation and cohesion (-1 to 1),"Good >0.5, Moderate >0.25, Poor <0.25"
Core Quality,Davies-Bouldin Index,1.100000,Cluster similarity (lower is better),"Excellent <0.5, Good <1.0, Fair <2.0, Poor >2.0"
Core Quality,Calinski-Harabasz Index,185.00,Between-cluster dispersion (higher is better),Context dependent
Feature Distribution,Within-Cluster CV,0.150000,Average coefficient of variation within clusters,Lower values indicate tighter clusters
Feature Distribution,Between-Cluster CV,0.450000,Average coefficient of variation between clusters,Higher values indicate better separation
Feature Distribution,Within-Cluster CV Std,0.030000,Standard deviation of within-cluster CV,Lower values indicate more consistent clusters
Feature Distribution,Between-Cluster CV Std,0.080000,Standard deviation of between-cluster CV,Lower values indicate more consistent separation
Feature Distribution,Per-Regime CV Values,"{0: 0.12, 1: 0.18, 2: 0.14, 3: 0.16}",CV values for each individual regime,Shows variation across different regimes
Cluster Structure,Number of Regimes,4,Total number of regimes discovered,Optimal range depends on data complexity
Cluster Structure,Noise Ratio,0.0000,Ratio of noise points (-1 labels),Lower values indicate cleaner clustering
Cluster Structure,Balance Score,0.9200,"Cluster balance measure (0-1, higher is better)",Values closer to 1 indicate more balanced clusters
Cluster Structure,Cluster Size Distribution,"[0.24, 0.26, 0.23, 0.27]",Size distribution across clusters,Balanced distributions are preferable
Temporal Analysis,Temporal Smoothness,0.8800,Regime persistence over time (0-1),"High >0.8, Medium >0.6, Low <0.6"
Temporal Analysis,Regime Persistence,28.50,Average regime duration in periods,Higher values indicate more stable regimes
Economic Validation,Economic Validation Available,Yes,Economic metrics calculated for each regime,See detailed economic analysis in report
Economic Summary,Mean Return Range,-0.00180 to 0.00420,Range of mean returns across regimes,Wider range indicates better regime separation
Economic Summary,Sharpe Ratio Range,-0.8200 to 2.3300,Range of Sharpe ratios across regimes,Positive values indicate profitable regimes
Economic Summary,Hit Rate Range,0.450 to 0.720,Range of hit rates across regimes,Higher values indicate more predictable regimes
Economic Summary,Max Drawdown Range,-0.1500 to -0.0600,Range of maximum drawdowns across regimes,Less negative values indicate lower risk
Predictive Power,Predictive Power Score,0.7300,Cross-validation accuracy for regime prediction,Higher values indicate more predictable regimes
Model Validation,Log Likelihood,-1450.00,Model log likelihood,Higher (less negative) values indicate better fit
Model Validation,Refit Stability ARI,0.8500,Stability of clustering on refit (0-1),Higher values indicate more stable clustering
Model Validation,Occupancy Entropy,1.3800,Entropy of state occupancy distribution,Higher values indicate more diverse regime usage
Configuration,Method Parameters,"{'K': 4, 'base_alpha': 0.75, 'kappa': 18.5, 'n_mixtures': 2, 'pca_components': 15, 'learning_rate': 0.045, 'svi_iterations': 1200}",Clustering method hyperparameters,See detailed configuration in analysis
